.TH MARBOR\-MODEL-CONFIG 1 "2026-08-17" "marbor dev" "Marbor Manual"
.SH NAME
marbor\-model-config \- manage per\-node model parameter profiles (P\-A2-06b)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B marbor model\-config
[action] [args] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
store.ModelConfig has ~40 optional per\-runtime sampling/load\-time fields, so
"set" takes a JSON body via \-\-from-json (a literal JSON string or
@path/to/file.json) rather than dozens of individual flags - see
internal/cli/modelconfig.go for the full field list and rationale.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B get
get a model's parameter profile on one node
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-model string
model name (required) (required)
.TP
.B \-\-node string
node name (required) (required)
.RE
.TP
.B set
create/update a model's parameter profile (full JSON body)
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-from-json string
JSON body (literal string, or @path/to/file.json) - must include "model" and "node" (required) (required)
.RE
.TP
.B delete
reset a model on a node to backend defaults
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-model string
model name (required) (required)
.TP
.B \-\-node string
node name (required) (required)
.RE
.TP
.B list
list every configured model parameter profile
.TP
.B capabilities
show which parameter fields take effect per runtime
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-server
Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MARBOR_SERVER)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of a human table
.TP
.B \-\-username
admin username, used to log in (env MARBOR_USERNAME)
.TP
.B \-\-password
admin password, used to log in (env MARBOR_PASSWORD)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmarbor\fR(1)
